    <string name="audio_algorithm_extrastereo_description" formatted="false">"FFmpeg extrastereo boosts the channel difference across the full range. Mono stays mono."</string>
    <string name="audio_algorithm_stereowiden_description" formatted="false">"FFmpeg stereowiden combines negative crossfeed with a short delay. Start with a moderate effect mix."</string>
    <string name="audio_algorithm_haas_description" formatted="false">"FFmpeg Haas creates width through short delays of the center signal. At 100% wet it replaces the original side component, so use a moderate mix."</string>
    <string name="audio_algorithm_allpass_description" formatted="false">"StereoWidener allpass changes phase relationships using all-pass filters. Lower and upper bands have separate controls."</string>
    <string name="audio_algorithm_velvet_description" formatted="false">"StereoWidener velvet noise creates channel differences using sparse impulses. Lower and upper bands have separate controls."</string>
    <string name="audio_algorithm_multiband_description" formatted="false">"Independent M/S width for low, mid and high frequencies. 100% in each band is the original width. It cannot create width from mono."</string>
    <string name="audio_algorithm_pae_description" formatted="false">"PAE/PAD separates the directional part from ambience and mainly widens the ambience. This is an estimate from stereo, not instrument separation."</string>
    <string name="audio_algorithm_side_description" formatted="false">"Creates a decorrelated side component from the center while preserving the original Mid and Side. Also works with mono; the resulting space is artificial."</string>
    <string name="audio_algorithm_shuffler_description" formatted="false">"Stereo Shuffler changes the frequency balance of center and side components, redistributing width across the spectrum without delayed echoes."</string>
    <string name="audio_algorithm_micropitch_description" formatted="false">"MicroPitch adds slightly detuned copies of the channels with short delays. This creative effect changes the sound of the recording."</string>
    <string name="audio_algorithm_ms_description" formatted="false">"M/S changes the balance of center and side components while preserving low frequencies. It cannot create additional width from mono."</string>
